        "original_id": "fe9663d5-06d8-5f17-a5c4-a1f29569109b",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Ludwig Friedrich Leopold von Gerlach, Otto von Bismarck, Ernst Ludwig von Gerlach, Frederick William IV of Prussia, Carl Friedrich Leopold von Gerlach\n- Roles: Prussian army general, adjutant, Protestant conservative, conservative Prussian statesman\n\nFacts:\n- Ludwig Friedrich Leopold von Gerlach was born on 17 September 1790 and died on 10 January 1861.\n- Otto von Bismarck was born on 1 April 1815 and died on 30 July 1898.\n- Ludwig Friedrich Leopold von Gerlach was a Prussian army general, an adjutant to Frederick William IV of Prussia, and a Protestant conservative associate of Otto von Bismarck.\n- Otto von Bismarck, also styled Prince of Bismarck and Duke of Lauenburg, was a conservative Prussian statesman who dominated German and European affairs from the 1860s until 1890.\n- Ernst Ludwig von Gerlach was the son of Carl Friedrich Leopold von Gerlach and the brother of Ludwig Friedrich Leopold von Gerlach.",
